-- title:
--   Normalized eigenform in a Hecke-stable subspace supporting a prime
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ and let $S$ be an arbitrary set of natural numbers. Write $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ for the space of weight-$2$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$, and let $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) be the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators [`CuspForm.heckeTLin 2`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperatorForms.html#L69) attached to primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators [`CuspForm.heckeULin 2`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperatorForms.html#L83) attached to primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$, these being the usual operators defined by the slash-action coset sums $U_p f = \sum_{j<p} f\mid_k \gamma_{p,j}$ and $T_p f = U_p f + f \mid_k \operatorname{diag}(p)$. Let $W$ be a $\mathbb C$-subspace of $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ that is stable under `heckeTLin 2` for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ and under `heckeULin 2` for every prime $\ell \mid N$ (all such primes, irrespective of $S$). Let $\mathfrak p \subset \mathbb T$ be a prime ideal containing the annihilator of $W$, i.e. such that every $t \in \mathbb T$ acting by $0$ on all of $W$ lies in $\mathfrak p$. Then there is an $f \in W$ satisfying `IsNormalizedEigenform`, that is: its $q$-expansion coefficients $a_n =$ `qCoeff f n` (taken with width $1$) satisfy $a_1 = 1$, $a_{mn} = a_m a_n$ for coprime $m,n$, $a_{p^{r+2}} = a_p a_{p^{r+1}} - p\, a_{p^r}$ for primes $p \nmid N$, and $a_{p^{r+2}} = a_p a_{p^{r+1}}$ for primes $p \mid N$; and such that every $t \in \mathbb T$ with $t f = 0$ lies in $\mathfrak p$.
--
--   This is the subspace form of the Deligne–Serre eigenform-realisation lemma: a prime of the Hecke algebra whose support meets a Hecke-stable subspace $W$ is realised by a normalized eigenform lying in $W$ itself. It is used in the construction of newforms attached to primes of the Hecke algebra, being cited by [`CuspForm.exists_isNormalizedEigenform_isNewAt_of_heckeAlgebra_support`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_isNormalizedEigenform_isNewAt_of_heckeAlgebra_support).
-- source:
